  "body": "**What changed**\r\n\r\n- A `.mch` file can state `controller.post`, the name of a built-in post. `Machine.post`\r\n  holds it. A file without the key reads as before.\r\n- The reader refuses a value that is not a non-empty string, at `controller.post`\r\n  (`post::machine::post_name`).\r\n- The validator also refuses a name that is not a built-in post, and a post that does not\r\n  serve the machine's kind. The post crate gets the registry as a closure, as the holder\r\n  lookup does (#828), so there is no new crate edge.\r\n- `posting::post_offer` returns `Option<PostOffer>`. It offers the machine's named post\r\n  (`OfferWhy::Machine`) when that post is in the registry, serves the mount, and is not\r\n  the setup's post. Otherwise it gives the kind offer as before (`OfferWhy::Kind`). A\r\n  `.cps` file post is never offered over.\r\n- The Setup page's banner tells which offer it is: \"the machine names grblHAL as its post;\r\n  switch to it?\" or the kind text as before. The button queues `SelectPostNamed`, so it\r\n  rides undo.\r\n- A mount never changes the post by itself (#343, #388).\r\n- The MCP tools say the same, after the QA finding on #2374. `post_offer_for` asks for any\r\n  setup (`posting_offer.rs`). `load_machine` replies with `post_offer` for the setup that it\r\n  mounted to, and `get_job` gives `post_offer` for each setup: the post, why, and the\r\n  `set_setup_post` call that takes it. `null` means no offer.\r\n- The description of the `post` tool lists every name in `BUILTINS`. The hand-written list\r\n  did not have \"Tormach PathPilot\", grblHAL, TinyG or the Carvera posts.\r\n- 32 shipped machine files state their post, where `MACHINES`, a machine's issue or its\r\n  post writes the pairing: the PathPilot mills, routers, lathes and plasma table, grblHAL\r\n  and the Sienci AltMills, TinyG, the Makera machines, the Doosan DNM 5700s and the Haas\r\n  machines. The generic machines, the Sodick ALC400G, the Mach3-era Tormach mills and the\r\n  sinker template state none.\r\n- The Machines pane's file editor gives a user's own machine its post. General has a Post\r\n  row, a dropdown (`Field.choices`) of the built-in posts that serve the file's kind, plus\r\n  \"(none)\", which takes the key out. A stated name off the list stays in view with its\r\n  refusal. Only built-in posts are offered: a `.cps` file has no stable name for a machine\r\n  file to state.\r\n- `assets/machines/AGENTS.md` documents the key.\r\n- Decision file: `docs/decisions/2374-machine-names-its-post.md`.\r\n\r\n**Screenshots**\r\n\r\nTaken by hand in the Windows release build. \"Before\" is a build of `main` from before this\r\nbranch; \"after\" is this PR's head `b6bc94239`. Same document, setup and window in each pair.\r\nThe path line under \"Editing ...\" is masked: it showed a local user folder.\r\n\r\n| | Before | After |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Setup page, Post: a setup on the shipped Tormach 770MX with the Fanuc post | ![Setup Post before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/roer70/Camcraft/c15c4c720e0f6a3c4265d3c998afeb3ad0904e46/2554/setup-banner-before.png) | ![Setup Post after: the machine names Tormach PathPilot as its post; switch to it?](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/roer70/Camcraft/c15c4c720e0f6a3c4265d3c998afeb3ad0904e46/2554/setup-banner-after.png) |\r\n| Machines pane, file editor, General: a user's own grblHAL machine | ![Machines editor before: no Post row](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/roer70/Camcraft/c15c4c720e0f6a3c4265d3c998afeb3ad0904e46/2554/machine-editor-before.png) | ![Machines editor after: a Post row](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/roer70/Camcraft/c15c4c720e0f6a3c4265d3c998afeb3ad0904e46/2554/machine-editor-after.png) |\r\n\r\nThe Post dropdown open, after: \"(none)\" and the built-in posts that serve a mill.\r\n\r\n![Machines editor after: the Post dropdown open](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/roer70/Camcraft/c15c4c720e0f6a3c4265d3c998afeb3ad0904e46/2554/machine-editor-after-open.png)\r\n\r\n**Readings**\r\n\r\nBranched from `main` at `6349a542e`.\r\n\r\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, 346 steps, 0 failed, on `2d26ef2a3`.\r\n- `cargo xtask gate batch --base upstream/main`: 837 steps, 836 ok, 61.9 min. The one red step was\r\n  `clippy -D warnings` (`bool::then` with a closure in `posting_offer.rs`), fixed in\r\n  `a9205467b`; that step reran green with `--failed`.\r\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on the head `b6bc94239`, clean tree: green,\r\n  346 steps, 0 failed, 10.0 min.\r\n- By hand, the release build: a setup on the grblHAL machine is offered the grblHAL post\r\n  and the switch rides undo; a user's own machine picks its post from the editor's dropdown,\r\n  writes it, and the Setup page then offers it.\r\n\r\n**Pinning tests**\r\n\r\n- `crates/app/tests/machine_library.rs`:\r\n  `a_machine_that_names_its_post_is_offered_it_and_the_choice_rides_undo`,\r\n  `the_named_post_must_be_a_built_in_post_that_serves_the_machine`,\r\n  `the_editor_offers_the_built_in_posts_that_serve_the_machine`\r\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/machine_named_post.rs`:\r\n  `the_grblhal_machine_offers_its_own_post_and_the_switch_rides_undo`,\r\n  `a_users_own_machine_picks_its_post_from_the_editors_dropdown`\r\n- `crates/app/tests/mcp_machine_post.rs`:\r\n  `mounting_the_770mx_offers_pathpilot_and_the_agent_takes_it_as_one_undo_step`,\r\n  `the_offer_follows_the_setup_the_machine_went_to_not_the_active_one`,\r\n  `a_machine_that_names_no_post_and_serves_the_current_one_offers_nothing`,\r\n  `the_post_tool_lists_every_registry_post`\r\n- `crates/post/src/machine/post_name.rs`: five unit tests for the reader and the rule.\r\n- Not changed and still green: the lathe-over-mill-post offer test in\r\n  `ui/src/egui_app/tests.rs`, `plasma_post.rs` (only moved to `offer.post`) and\r\n  `sinker_burn.rs`.\r\n\r\n**Not exercised**\r\n\r\n- By hand: a `.cps` file post on the setup is not offered over. The tests pin it.\r\n- An older reader on a new file. `Machine` is `#[serde(default)]`, so an older reader drops\r\n  the key and loses only the offer, never a posted line. Thus no `PROJECT_VERSION` bump.\r\n- The pairing for machines with no written pairing. They state no post, and the kind offer\r\n  does not change for them.\r\n- An MCP agent on a document without setups. The `set_setup_post` refusal names\r\n  `select_post`, which is not an MCP tool; the offer's hint says `add_setup`, then\r\n  `set_setup_post`. The refusal text did not change here.\r\n\r\nChangelog: A machine file can name the post that writes its programs; the Setup page and the MCP `load_machine` and `get_job` replies offer that post, the Machines editor picks it from a dropdown, the `post` tool lists every built-in post, and the shipped grblHAL, PathPilot, TinyG, Makera, Doosan and Haas machines name theirs (#2374)\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\nFixes #2374\r\n",
